    "q-216769": {
      "dom_id": "step-q216769",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Select the correct options in the truth table below and use this to determine whether $(¬A∧B)∧(A∧¬B)$ is a contradiction.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∧B\\,$ | $\\,A∧¬B\\,$ | $\\,(¬A∧B)∧(A∧¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |\n\nAccording to the table, $(¬A∧B)∧(A∧¬B)$ \n{{field-5}}\nalways false. Therefore, it \n{{field-6}} \na contradiction.",
      "worked_solution": "An expression is a contradiction if it is always false, regardless of the inputs.\n\nBy completing the final column in the truth table below, we obtain the following:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∧B\\,$ | $\\,A∧¬B\\,$ | $\\,(¬A∧B)∧(A∧¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nAccording to the table, $(¬A∧B)∧(A∧¬B)$ \n$\\text{is}$\nalways false. Therefore, it \n$\\text{is}$\na contradiction.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
